{"programs":[{"id":"ss-lp","name":"Novice Linear Progression","short":"Novice LP","credit":"Modeled on Starting Strength (Mark Rippetoe)","url":"https://startingstrength.com","level":"beginner","daysPerWeek":3,"focus":["strength","functional"],"summary":"Three full-body sessions a week alternating A and B. Squat every session, press and bench alternate, one heavy set of deadlift. The simplest proven way to get strong fast.","progression":"Add weight every session: about 5 lb / 2.5 kg on presses, 10 lb / 5 kg on squat and deadlift early on, then 5 lb. When you miss reps three sessions in a row, deload 10% and build back.","days":[{"name":"Workout A","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Squat","name":"Barbell Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"Standing_Military_Press","name":"Standing Military Press","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Deadlift","name":"Barbell Deadlift","mode":"strength","sets":1,"reps":"5","restSec":240,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}}]},{"name":"Workout B","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Squat","name":"Barbell Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip","name":"Barbell Bench Press - Medium Grip","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Power_Clean","name":"Power Clean","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"3","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}}]}]},{"id":"sl-5x5","name":"StrongLifts 5×5","short":"5×5","credit":"Mehdi, StrongLifts","url":"https://stronglifts.com","level":"beginner","daysPerWeek":3,"focus":["strength"],"summary":"Two alternating full-body workouts, three days a week, five sets of five on the big barbell lifts. Rows and the overhead press make it a touch more upper-body focused than Starting Strength.","progression":"Add 5 lb / 2.5 kg every workout (10 lb / 5 kg on deadlift). Fail a weight three times, deload 10% on that lift.","days":[{"name":"Workout A","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Squat","name":"Barbell Squat","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip","name":"Barbell Bench Press - Medium Grip","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Bent_Over_Barbell_Row","name":"Bent Over Barbell Row","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}}]},{"name":"Workout B","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Squat","name":"Barbell Squat","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Standing_Military_Press","name":"Standing Military Press","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Deadlift","name":"Barbell Deadlift","mode":"strength","sets":1,"reps":"5","restSec":240,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}}]}]},{"id":"gzclp","name":"GZCLP","short":"GZCLP","credit":"Cody Lefever (GZCL method)","url":"https://www.gzcl.com","level":"beginner","daysPerWeek":3,"focus":["strength","upper"],"summary":"Linear progression with three tiers per day: a heavy T1 lift for 5×3 with an AMRAP last set, a moderate T2 for 3×10, and a light T3 for 3×15+. Four workouts rotate, so you run it three or four days a week.","progression":"T1 and T2: add 5 lb / 2.5 kg upper, 10 lb / 5 kg lower each time you complete all sets. When you fail T1 5×3, move to 6×2, then 10×1, then reset. T3: add weight once the last set hits 25 reps.","days":[{"name":"A1","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Squat","name":"Barbell Squat","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"3 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip","name":"Barbell Bench Press - Medium Grip","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":120,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Wide-Grip_Lat_Pulldown","name":"Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":60}]},{"name":"B1","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Standing_Military_Press","name":"Standing Military Press","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"3 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Deadlift","name":"Barbell Deadlift","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":120,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"One-Arm_Dumbbell_Row","name":"One-Arm Dumbbell Row","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":60}]},{"name":"A2","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip","name":"Barbell Bench Press - Medium Grip","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"3 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Squat","name":"Barbell Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":120,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"Wide-Grip_Lat_Pulldown","name":"Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":60}]},{"name":"B2","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Deadlift","name":"Barbell Deadlift","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"3 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"Standing_Military_Press","name":"Standing Military Press","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":120,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"One-Arm_Dumbbell_Row","name":"One-Arm Dumbbell Row","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":60}]}]},{"id":"reddit-ppl","name":"Push / Pull / Legs","short":"PPL","credit":"Metallicadpa, r/Fitness beginner PPL","url":"https://thefitness.wiki/routines/metallicadpa-ppl/","level":"beginner","daysPerWeek":6,"focus":["upper","hypertrophy"],"summary":"Six days a week, each muscle twice. One heavy compound with an AMRAP last set, then accessories for 8–12 and 15–20 reps. The classic upper-body builder. Run 3 days a week if 6 is too much.","progression":"Add 5 lb / 2.5 kg to the main lift every session (10 lb / 5 kg on deadlift) as long as the AMRAP set hits 5+. Accessories: add weight when you reach the top of the rep range on every set.","days":[{"name":"Pull A","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Deadlift","name":"Barbell Deadlift","mode":"strength","sets":1,"reps":"5 (AMRAP)","restSec":240,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"Wide-Grip_Lat_Pulldown","name":"Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Seated_Cable_Rows","name":"Seated Cable Rows","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Face_Pull","name":"Face Pull","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"15-20","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Hammer_Curls","name":"Hammer Curls","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Dumbbell_Bicep_Curl","name":"Dumbbell Bicep Curl","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60}]},{"name":"Push A","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip","name":"Barbell Bench Press - Medium Grip","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"5 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Standing_Military_Press","name":"Standing Military Press","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Incline_Dumbbell_Press","name":"Incline Dumbbell Press","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Triceps_Pushdown_-_Rope_Attachment","name":"Triceps Pushdown - Rope Attachment","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Cable_Rope_Overhead_Triceps_Extension","name":"Cable Rope Overhead Triceps Extension","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Side_Lateral_Raise","name":"Side Lateral Raise","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15-20","restSec":60}]},{"name":"Legs","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Squat","name":"Barbell Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Romanian_Deadlift","name":"Romanian Deadlift","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Leg_Press","name":"Leg Press","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Seated_Leg_Curl","name":"Seated Leg Curl","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Standing_Calf_Raises","name":"Standing Calf Raises","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60}]},{"name":"Pull B","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Bent_Over_Barbell_Row","name":"Bent Over Barbell Row","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"5 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Wide-Grip_Lat_Pulldown","name":"Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Seated_Cable_Rows","name":"Seated Cable Rows","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Face_Pull","name":"Face Pull","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"15-20","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Hammer_Curls","name":"Hammer Curls","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Dumbbell_Bicep_Curl","name":"Dumbbell Bicep Curl","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60}]},{"name":"Push B","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Standing_Military_Press","name":"Standing Military Press","mode":"strength","sets":5,"reps":"5 (last set AMRAP)","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip","name":"Barbell Bench Press - Medium Grip","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Incline_Dumbbell_Press","name":"Incline Dumbbell Press","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Triceps_Pushdown_-_Rope_Attachment","name":"Triceps Pushdown - Rope Attachment","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Cable_Rope_Overhead_Triceps_Extension","name":"Cable Rope Overhead Triceps Extension","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Side_Lateral_Raise","name":"Side Lateral Raise","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15-20","restSec":60}]}]},{"id":"upper-lower","name":"Upper / Lower","short":"U/L","credit":"Common 4-day template (PHUL-style power + hypertrophy days)","level":"intermediate","daysPerWeek":4,"focus":["upper","strength","hypertrophy"],"summary":"Two upper and two lower days a week: one heavy, one higher-rep each. More recovery than PPL, more upper-body volume than a full-body program.","progression":"Power days: add weight when you get all sets at the target reps. Hypertrophy days: work in the rep range and add weight at the top of it.","days":[{"name":"Upper Power","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip","name":"Barbell Bench Press - Medium Grip","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Bent_Over_Barbell_Row","name":"Bent Over Barbell Row","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Standing_Military_Press","name":"Standing Military Press","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Pullups","name":"Pullups","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Curl","name":"Barbell Curl","mode":"strength","sets":2,"reps":"10","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"EZ-Bar_Skullcrusher","name":"EZ-Bar Skullcrusher","mode":"strength","sets":2,"reps":"10","restSec":60}]},{"name":"Lower Power","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Squat","name":"Barbell Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"Romanian_Deadlift","name":"Romanian Deadlift","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8","restSec":150,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Leg_Press","name":"Leg Press","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Standing_Calf_Raises","name":"Standing Calf Raises","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Hanging_Leg_Raise","name":"Hanging Leg Raise","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"12","restSec":60}]},{"name":"Upper Hypertrophy","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Incline_Dumbbell_Press","name":"Incline Dumbbell Press","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Seated_Cable_Rows","name":"Seated Cable Rows","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Side_Lateral_Raise","name":"Side Lateral Raise","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Face_Pull","name":"Face Pull","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Hammer_Curls","name":"Hammer Curls","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Triceps_Pushdown","name":"Triceps Pushdown","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Dips_-_Chest_Version","name":"Dips - Chest Version","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"AMRAP","restSec":90}]},{"name":"Lower Hypertrophy","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Front_Barbell_Squat","name":"Front Barbell Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8","restSec":150},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Hip_Thrust","name":"Barbell Hip Thrust","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Dumbbell_Lunges","name":"Dumbbell Lunges","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10 / leg","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Lying_Leg_Curls","name":"Lying Leg Curls","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Seated_Calf_Raise","name":"Seated Calf Raise","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"15","restSec":60}]}]},{"id":"bwf-rr","name":"Bodyweight Recommended Routine","short":"RR","credit":"r/bodyweightfitness community","url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/bodyweightfitness/wiki/kb/recommended_routine/","level":"beginner","daysPerWeek":3,"focus":["functional","bodyweight","balance","upper"],"summary":"Full-body calisthenics three times a week: a pull, a push, a squat and a hinge pattern, each paired, plus a core triplet. Progress by moving to a harder variation, not by adding plates. Great for balance and control.","progression":"Work 3 sets of 5–8. When you hit 3×8 cleanly, move to the next harder variation (for example push-up → diamond push-up → pseudo-planche push-up). Holds: add 5–10 seconds.","days":[{"name":"Full Body","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"x-dead-hang","name":"Dead Hang","mode":"timed","sets":1,"reps":"30 s","restSec":30},{"exerciseId":"x-deep-squat-hold","name":"Deep Squat Hold","mode":"timed","sets":1,"reps":"45 s","restSec":30},{"exerciseId":"x-wall-slides","name":"Wall Slides","mode":"strength","sets":1,"reps":"10","restSec":30},{"exerciseId":"Pullups","name":"Pullups","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5-8","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Dips_-_Chest_Version","name":"Dips - Chest Version","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5-8","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Inverted_Row","name":"Inverted Row","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5-8","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Pushups","name":"Pushups","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5-8","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"x-pistol-squat","name":"Pistol Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5-8 / leg","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"x-nordic-curl","name":"Nordic Hamstring Curl","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5-8","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Hanging_Leg_Raise","name":"Hanging Leg Raise","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8-12","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"x-copenhagen-plank","name":"Copenhagen Plank","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"30 s / side","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"x-hollow-hold","name":"Hollow Body Hold","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"30 s","restSec":60}]}]},{"id":"simple-sinister","name":"Simple & Sinister","short":"S&S","credit":"Pavel Tsatsouline, StrongFirst","url":"https://www.strongfirst.com/sinister/","level":"beginner","daysPerWeek":5,"focus":["functional","kettlebell","balance"],"summary":"The minimalist kettlebell practice: 100 one-arm swings in sets of 10 and 10 Turkish get-ups, most days of the week. Builds a strong hinge, grip, shoulders and whole-body control in about 30 minutes.","progression":"Stay with a bell until the full session feels easy within 5 minutes for swings and 10 for get-ups, then move up one bell size on one movement at a time. Never grind.","days":[{"name":"Daily Practice","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Goblet_Squat","name":"Goblet Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":45},{"exerciseId":"Butt_Lift_Bridge","name":"Butt Lift (Bridge)","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":45},{"exerciseId":"One-Arm_Kettlebell_Swings","name":"One-Arm Kettlebell Swings","mode":"strength","sets":10,"reps":"10 (alternate hands)","restSec":30,"progress":{"lb":8,"kg":4}},{"exerciseId":"Kettlebell_Turkish_Get-Up_Lunge_style","name":"Kettlebell Turkish Get-Up (Lunge style)","mode":"strength","sets":10,"reps":"1 (alternate sides)","restSec":45,"progress":{"lb":8,"kg":4}}]}]},{"id":"daily-mobility","name":"Daily Mobility","short":"Mobility","credit":"Inspired by Joe DeFranco’s Limber 11 and Agile 8","level":"beginner","daysPerWeek":7,"focus":["mobility","balance"],"summary":"A 15-minute hip, spine and shoulder routine to do most days or before lifting. Hinge, squat and overhead positions all open up, and the holds double as a progress log.","progression":"Add 10–15 seconds to holds and a rep or two to the movement drills as positions get easier. Depth and comfort are the goal, not load.","days":[{"name":"Mobility 15","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"x-cat-cow","name":"Cat-Cow","mode":"strength","sets":2,"reps":"10","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"Worlds_Greatest_Stretch","name":"World's Greatest Stretch","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"5 / side","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-90-90","name":"90/90 Hip Switch","mode":"strength","sets":2,"reps":"8 / side","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-couch-stretch","name":"Couch Stretch","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"45 s / side","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-deep-squat-hold","name":"Deep Squat Hold","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"45 s","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-frog-stretch","name":"Frog Stretch","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"45 s","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-open-book","name":"Thoracic Open Book","mode":"strength","sets":2,"reps":"8 / side","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-pigeon-pose","name":"Pigeon Pose","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"45 s / side","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-cossack-squat","name":"Cossack Squat","mode":"strength","sets":2,"reps":"8 / side","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-dead-hang","name":"Dead Hang","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"30 s","restSec":30}]}]},{"id":"upper-functional","name":"Upper-Focus Functional","short":"UFF","credit":"Macro Log template built around pressing, pulling, carries and single-leg balance","level":"intermediate","daysPerWeek":3,"focus":["functional","upper","balance"],"summary":"Three days built around one heavy upper-body lift each, with get-ups, carries, single-leg work and holds for balance and core. Strength you can feel outside the gym.","progression":"Add 5 lb / 2.5 kg to the main press or pull when all sets hit the target. For single-leg and balance work, add reps or hold time first, then load.","days":[{"name":"Day A · Press & balance","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Standing_Military_Press","name":"Standing Military Press","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Kettlebell_Turkish_Get-Up_Lunge_style","name":"Kettlebell Turkish Get-Up (Lunge style)","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"1 / side","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Dips_-_Chest_Version","name":"Dips - Chest Version","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"x-single-leg-rdl","name":"Single-Leg Romanian Deadlift","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8 / leg","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Side_Lateral_Raise","name":"Side Lateral Raise","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"x-copenhagen-plank","name":"Copenhagen Plank","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"30 s / side","restSec":60}]},{"name":"Day B · Pull & hinge","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Pullups","name":"Pullups","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"6","restSec":150},{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Deadlift","name":"Barbell Deadlift","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5","restSec":240,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"One-Arm_Dumbbell_Row","name":"One-Arm Dumbbell Row","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":90},{"exerciseId":"Face_Pull","name":"Face Pull","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"15","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"Farmers_Walk","name":"Farmer's Walk","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"40 s","restSec":90,"progress":{"lb":10,"kg":5}},{"exerciseId":"x-hollow-hold","name":"Hollow Body Hold","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"30 s","restSec":60}]},{"name":"Day C · Bench & legs","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Barbell_Bench_Press_-_Medium_Grip","name":"Barbell Bench Press - Medium Grip","mode":"strength","sets":4,"reps":"5","restSec":180,"progress":{"lb":5,"kg":2.5}},{"exerciseId":"Goblet_Squat","name":"Goblet Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"10","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"x-pistol-squat","name":"Pistol Squat","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"5 / leg","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"Chin-Up","name":"Chin-Up","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"8","restSec":120},{"exerciseId":"x-hip-airplane","name":"Hip Airplane","mode":"strength","sets":3,"reps":"6 / side","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"x-wall-handstand","name":"Wall Handstand Hold","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"20 s","restSec":90}]}]},{"id":"yoga-balance","name":"Yoga & Balance Progress","short":"Yoga","credit":"Macro Log template","level":"beginner","daysPerWeek":2,"focus":["yoga","balance","mobility"],"summary":"A check-in practice for poses you want to progress. Log how long you hold each one; the exercise page charts your best hold over time, so crow, headstand and handstand become measurable.","progression":"Chase longer, calmer holds. Add 5 seconds when a hold feels steady; for inversions, go from wall-assisted to free-standing before adding time.","days":[{"name":"Balance & inversions","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"x-tree-pose","name":"Tree Pose","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"30 s / side","restSec":15},{"exerciseId":"x-warrior-3","name":"Warrior III","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"20 s / side","restSec":15},{"exerciseId":"x-half-moon","name":"Half Moon Pose","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"20 s / side","restSec":15},{"exerciseId":"x-crow-pose","name":"Crow Pose","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"10 s","restSec":45},{"exerciseId":"x-headstand","name":"Headstand","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"20 s","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"x-wall-handstand","name":"Wall Handstand Hold","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"20 s","restSec":60},{"exerciseId":"x-boat-pose","name":"Boat Pose","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"30 s","restSec":30}]},{"name":"Flexibility & backbends","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"x-downward-dog","name":"Downward Dog","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"45 s","restSec":15},{"exerciseId":"x-chair-pose","name":"Chair Pose","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"45 s","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-wheel-pose","name":"Wheel Pose","mode":"timed","sets":3,"reps":"15 s","restSec":45},{"exerciseId":"x-bridge-pose","name":"Bridge Pose","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"30 s","restSec":20},{"exerciseId":"x-pigeon-pose","name":"Pigeon Pose","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"60 s / side","restSec":15},{"exerciseId":"x-forward-fold","name":"Standing Forward Fold","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"45 s","restSec":15},{"exerciseId":"Plank","name":"Plank","mode":"timed","sets":2,"reps":"60 s","restSec":30}]}]},{"id":"zone2-base","name":"Zone 2 Base","short":"Zone 2","credit":"Macro Log template","level":"beginner","daysPerWeek":3,"focus":["cardio"],"summary":"Three easy aerobic sessions a week at a pace where you can still talk. The cheapest investment in recovery, heart health and work capacity for lifting.","progression":"Add 5 minutes to one session a week until you reach 45–60 minutes, then nudge the pace.","days":[{"name":"Easy run","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"x-run","name":"Running (outdoor)","mode":"cardio","sets":1,"reps":"30 min","restSec":0}]},{"name":"Bike or row","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"Bicycling_Stationary","name":"Bicycling, Stationary","mode":"cardio","sets":1,"reps":"40 min","restSec":0}]},{"name":"Long walk or hike","exercises":[{"exerciseId":"x-hike","name":"Hiking","mode":"cardio","sets":1,"reps":"60 min","restSec":0}]}]}]}